# PocketBase

PocketBase is the shared backend for the public site catalog and Stream Kit account auth.

| Consumer | Allowed use |
| --- | --- |
| `@stream-kit/site` | Server-side services for catalog, reviews, file URLs |
| `@stream-kit/app` (`packages/app/src/lib/core/auth`, `user-files`, `config-sync`) | Public JS client for `users` auth, `user_files`, and config sync collections |
| Plugins | Via `app.auth` only — never import `pocketbase` directly |

Do **not** put catalog CRUD, admin/superuser clients, or migrations in `packages/app` or plugins.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `site/pb/pb_migrations/` | Schema migrations (committed) |
| `site/pb/pb_hooks/` | JS hooks (committed) |
| `site/pb/pb_data/` | Local DB + uploads (gitignored) |
| `site/pb/pocketbase(.exe)` | Downloaded binary (gitignored) |
| `site/pb/PB_VERSION` | PocketBase binary version (shared by local setup + Docker) |
| `site/pb/package.json` | `@stream-kit/pocketbase` — changeset-versioned image package |
| `site/pb/Dockerfile` | Production image (binary + hooks + migrations) |
| `site/pb/docker-compose.yml` | Dockhand / Compose example with `pb_data` volume |
| `site/scripts/setup-pocketbase.mjs` | Downloads binary from `PB_VERSION` |
| `site/scripts/run-pocketbase.mjs` | Serves on `http://127.0.0.1:8090` |
| `site/scripts/seed-plugins.mjs` | Seeds plugins + uploads release zips to `files` |
| `packages/app/src/lib/core/auth/` | Desktop app auth service (`PUBLIC_POCKETBASE_URL`) |

Dev: root `pnpm dev` (or `pnpm dev:site`) starts PocketBase via `@stream-kit/pocketbase#dev` plus the site. Admin UI: `http://127.0.0.1:8090/_/`. Bootstrap creates `packages/app/.env` / `site/.env` and seeds a local `pro` plan when missing (see `site/scripts/run-pocketbase.mjs`). Seed refuses non-localhost URLs; use `SK_DEV_SEED=0` / `plan` / `full`. If port 8090 is already taken, the task exits so Turbo owns a single process.

App local env: set `PUBLIC_POCKETBASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090` in `packages/app/.env` (see `.env.example`; created automatically by `pnpm bootstrap`).

## Schema changes

- **Always** add a migration in `site/pb/pb_migrations/` — do not hand-edit `pb_data`.
- Start migrations with `/// <reference path="../pb_data/types.d.ts" />`.
- Use the `migrate(up, down)` pattern; keep collection IDs stable when editing existing migrations.
- Field names: **camelCase** (`streamKitVersion`, `isLatest`, `publishedAt`, `mimeType`).
- Document collection/field changes in `docs/site.md`.

### Collections

- **`users`** — default PocketBase auth collection (`avatar`, `name`, `email`, `password`, …). Shared by the desktop app and site marketplace.
- **`plugins`** — stable identity: `key` (unique), `name` (unique), `description`, `icon`, `author` → `_pb_users_auth_`, marketplace fields: `content` (markdown README), `category` (select), `tags` (multi-select), `averageRating`, `ratingCount`.
- **`files`** — release zips: `file` (upload), `mimeType`, `size`, `sha256`, `originalName` (metadata filled by `files.pb.js` hook).
- **`plugin_versions`** — releases linked to `plugins` (cascade delete): `version`, `streamKitVersion`, `entry`, `file` → `files`, `changelog`, `isLatest`, `publishedAt`. Unique on `(plugin, version)`.
- **`plugin_reviews`** — user ratings/comments: `plugin` → `plugins` (cascade), `user` → `users`, `rating` (1–5), `body`. Unique on `(plugin, user)`. Public read; create/update/delete requires auth and `user = @request.auth.id`.
- **`subscriptions`** — admin catalog of plans that unlock cloud features: `key` (unique), `name`, `description`, `icon`, `enabled`, `bullets` (JSON string array for plan card benefits), `maxFileBytes`, `maxStorageBytes`. Public list/view when `enabled = true`; write is superuser-only.
- **`user_subscriptions`** — membership history: `user` → `users`, `subscription` → `subscriptions`, `purchasedAt`, `cancelledAt`, **`endsAt`** (grace end after cancel), `status` (`active` \| `cancelled` \| `expired`). Users can list/view own rows; create/delete are superuser-only until purchase flows exist. Owners may cancel an active row (`status` → `cancelled`, set `endsAt` ≈ now + 30 days). Cloud entitlement = `status = "active"` **or** `status = "cancelled"` with `endsAt` still in the future.
- **`user_files`** — per-user cloud media: `user` → `users`, `file` (upload, **`protected: true`** — clients use `pb.files.getToken()` / `?token=` URLs), `mimeType`, `size`, `originalName`. Mime allowlist is media-only (no `application/octet-stream`). Owner-only list/view/delete. Create rule: authenticated only (multipart `user` body matching is brittle); `onRecordCreateRequest` forces `user` to auth id; `onRecordCreate` fills metadata and enforces plan `maxFileBytes` / `maxStorageBytes`. The desktop app stores **relative** `/api/files/...` paths in actions and resolves them against `PUBLIC_POCKETBASE_URL` at use time (with a cached file token). Marketplace release zips stay on **`files`**.
- **`user_action_queues`** / **`user_actions`** — cloud sync of queues/actions. Create rule: authenticated only; update/delete/list/view: owner. Hook `user_config_sync.pb.js` forces `user` to auth id and requires an **entitled** membership (active, or cancelled with `endsAt` in the future). Number fields that may be `0` (e.g. unlimited concurrency, sortOrder) are **not** marked required (PocketBase treats required numbers as nonzero). Monotone **`revision`** (number) drives LWW with `clientUpdatedAt` as tie-breaker; soft-deletes keep `revision` on the tombstone/remote row.
- **`user_overlays`** — published cloud browser sources. Stable public key is **`overlayId`** (local overlay UUID, unique). PocketBase **`id`** stays the default 15-char key (safer for file storage). Fields: `user`, `name`, `config` (JSON), `bundle` (zip of `dist/`, **not** protected, max 25MB), `published`, `revision`, `clientUpdatedAt`. Public list/view when `published = true` (also owner when authed). Create/update: authenticated; hook `user_overlays.pb.js` forces `user` + entitlement. The marketing/app **site** serves HTML at `/app/overlays/[uuid]/` (lookup by `overlayId`) — do not host overlay UI via PocketBase routes.

## SvelteKit integration (site)

- Talk to PocketBase **server-side only** via `site/src/lib/server/services/` (e.g. `PluginsService`).
- Wire services through `event.locals.services` in `site/src/lib/server/hooks/services.ts`.
- Default URL: `http://127.0.0.1:8090`. Do not expose admin tokens or superuser credentials to the client.
- Prefer `neverthrow` for service-layer error handling.
- Build file download URLs with `site/src/lib/server/pocketbase/file-url.ts`.

```typescript
// ✅ Server load / action
export const load = async ({ locals }) => {
	const result = await locals.services.plugins().listLatest();
	// ...
};

// ❌ Never import PocketBase admin client from +page.svelte or client code
```

## Desktop app auth

- Implement auth in `packages/app/src/lib/core/auth` with the public PocketBase SDK and `PUBLIC_POCKETBASE_URL` (`$env/static/public`, build-time).
- Persist the session with PocketBase `AsyncAuthStore` backed by the Tauri store (`app.auth.json`) — not `localStorage` (plugins share the same window origin).
- On boot: `authRefresh` **before** `authStore.onChange(..., true)` so consumers never start on a stale token. Wrap `pb.send` to retry once after `authRefresh` on 401; also refresh on a 30‑minute interval while signed in.
- Prefer `pb.filter('user={:id}', { id })` (and similar) over string-interpolated filters.
- Email changes use `requestEmailChange` (confirmation link); do not update `email` via the regular profile `update` call.
- After a password change, re-authenticate with `authWithPassword` because PocketBase rotates `tokenKey`.
- Expose `app.auth` to plugins (public profile: `id`, `name`, `avatarUrl`, `verified`, optional `subscription` `{ key, name, endsAt? }`).
- Never use `_superusers` or admin credentials from the app.

## Production hardening

- In PocketBase admin, **enable auth rate limits** for login/register (and related auth endpoints) before exposing production. See `docs/site.md`.
- Document collection/field changes in `docs/site.md` as well as this rule.

## Hooks

Place hook scripts in `site/pb/pb_hooks/`. Keep hooks focused; use migrations for schema, hooks for request/record lifecycle logic.

### Handler scope (isolated runtimes)

Every handler is serialized and executed in its own runtime, so it **cannot** access anything declared at the top level of the same `*.pb.js` file — that fails at runtime with `ReferenceError: helper is not defined`. Put shared helpers in `site/pb/pb_hooks/shared/*.js` (`module.exports = { … }`) and `require()` them **inside** the handler body:

```js
function requireActiveSubscription(e) {
	const entitlement = require(`${__hooks}/shared/entitlement.js`);
	const auth = entitlement.requestAuth(e);
	// …
	return e.next();
}
```

Globals (`$app`, `$dbx`, `BadRequestError`, `DynamicModel`, …) *are* available in handlers and required modules. Inline small constants inside the handler instead of hoisting them. `shared/` ships in the Docker image; `lib/` (schema codegen) is `.dockerignore`d, so never put runtime helpers there.

- **`shared/entitlement.js`** — membership entitlement (`hasEntitledMembership`, `findEntitledMembership`, `requestAuth`).
- **`shared/user-files.js`** — `user_files` mime allowlist, metadata, storage usage.
- **`shared/plugin-ratings.js`** — plugin rating aggregation.

- **`files.pb.js`** — on create/update of `files`, sets `mimeType`, `size`, `sha256`, and `originalName` from the uploaded file.
- **`user_files.pb.js`** — on create/update of `user_files`, sets metadata and enforces plan quotas.
- **`user_config_sync.pb.js`** — on create/update of `user_actions` / `user_action_queues`, requires auth + active subscription and forces `user` to the auth id.
- **`plugin_reviews.pb.js`** — after create/update/delete of `plugin_reviews`, recalculates `averageRating` and `ratingCount` on the parent plugin.

## Version bumps

When upgrading the PocketBase **binary**, update `site/pb/PB_VERSION`, delete the old local binary, and re-run `pnpm --filter @stream-kit/site pb:setup`. Bump `@stream-kit/pocketbase` via changesets so the Docker image rebuilds with the new binary.

When changing **hooks or migrations**, add a changeset for `@stream-kit/pocketbase` (`pnpm changeset`). After the version PR merges on `main`, `release.yml` triggers `publish-pocketbase.yml`, which pushes `ghcr.io/stream-kit-app/pocketbase` tagged with the package version (`0.1.1`, `v0.1.1`, `latest`). The workflow skips if that version tag already exists on GHCR.

### Production (Docker / Dockhand)

- Image: `ghcr.io/stream-kit-app/pocketbase` (production hooks + migrations baked in; **not** `pb_data`; excludes local schema codegen `main.pb.js` / `lib/` / …)
- Persist `/pb/pb_data` as a volume (see `site/pb/docker-compose.yml`)
- Dockhand: add GHCR (`https://ghcr.io`) with a PAT that has `read:packages` if the package is private
- Point the Cloudflare Tunnel at the container HTTP port (`8090`)
- First boot: create a superuser via admin installer logs or `pocketbase superuser create`
